# Hosts every VM with network policy can reach. One rule per line; see `devvm network allow --help`.
# Generic object storage and paste-like hosts are left out on purpose (easy ways to send data out);
# allow them per VM when a project needs them.

# Ubuntu and Debian packages (apt uses :80 and :443)
ports.ubuntu.com
archive.ubuntu.com
security.ubuntu.com
esm.ubuntu.com
deb.debian.org
security.debian.org
# Alpine's packages (--from alpine)
dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org

# mise's version lists, for versions a project's version files ask for (the downloads themselves are
# in each tool's policy)
mise-versions.jdx.dev
# The trust roots mise checks GitHub artifact attestations against (aqua tools such as pnpm): Sigstore's,
# for the attestations a project's release workflow signs, and GitHub's own, for its release
# attestations when the root built into mise is out of date
tuf-repo-cdn.sigstore.dev
tuf-repo.github.com
# Node's downloads, for the node a project's mise config asks for in a VM without the node toolchain
# (musl builds, on Alpine, come from unofficial-builds)
nodejs.org
unofficial-builds.nodejs.org

# GitHub: code, releases, tarballs, git over SSH
github.com
github.com:22
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
release-assets.githubusercontent.com
lfs.github.com
